From fba5a8287f62b5da375a5fe8f4fd9b5c563d294d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:04:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ac: ScanAPs finds made-up access points (Build 133)

The Denpa Men 2 (and other games that collect what they find around them)
scan for Wi-Fi access points with ac:u ScanAPs (0x001D), which Tangelo left
unimplemented, so they never found anything.

ScanAPs now answers with access points in the GetCurrentAPInfo layout
(0x34 each: SSID length, SSID, BSSID at 0x24, channel at 0x2C, signal at
0x2E) and their number in word 2. Field use from Denpa Men 2's code: it
makes its Denpa Men from the BSSID, skips one whose signal byte is below
0xA0 and skips locally administered BSSIDs.

The list comes from <sysdata>/access_points.txt when it exists (one per
line: SSID;BSSID[;signal], '#' comments). Without it there are 8 made-up
ones with real router vendor prefixes, the same all day and new the next
day, as for a console carried around.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
